{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>To count</b> — after the pattern of 'Make me know, YHWH, my end,' so 'give us a heart to know to count our days.' The meaning: that we may know their number is little, and we bring [it] into our midst, or bring a heart of wisdom upon us." "And behold, נביא — like: 'and what נביא to a man.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:48.505408620Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}